  "notes": "B.S. Electrical and Computer Engineering, College of Science and Engineering. QUARTER SYSTEM — all credits are quarter hours. Built from the official WWU Electrical and Computer Engineering department Plan of Study (https://wwu-eece.github.io/EECE%20Plan%20of%20Study.pdf, 'Year 2027', last updated March 2026; reflects the catalog for students starting Fall 2026). Major = 146 quarter credits excluding GURs: MATH 124/125/204/224/331, PHYS 161/162/163, CSCI 141, EECE 108/109/111/210/233/220/244/310/344/346/311/320/360/480/401, ENG 302 (writing proficiency), senior capstone EECE 402/403/404 (3cr each), 24cr Higher-Level EECE Electives (≥12cr in Year 3), 15cr Technical Electives (including 3cr math/basic science). GURs: QSR, LSCI/SCI, and writing proficiency met by major; remaining GURs (ACOM ENG 101, BCOM, HUM 12cr, SSC 12cr, ACGM, BCGM) modeled as choice slots. The official plan nominally totals 184cr (146 major + 38 GUR); WWU requires 180cr to graduate and EECE students typically enter with AP/IB/Running Start credit applying to GURs/electives or adjust technical electives with an advisor. EECE course credits at 4cr use the department standard where the plan PDF does not specify otherwise. 184 quarter credits total as specified by the official plan.",
